Experiment 10 - Storage backend comparison (JSON vs SQLite)
===========================================================
Protocol: 1000 synthetic accounts per backend, including concurrency and tampering.

+------------------------------------------------+--------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| Check                                          | Result | Detail                                                                |
+------------------------------------------------+--------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| json: all records readable                     | PASS   | 1000/1000                                                             |
| json: login uses the same auth logic           | PASS   |                                                                       |
| json: no concurrency errors                    | PASS   | 0                                                                     |
| json: concurrent updates all applied           | PASS   | counter=20/20                                                         |
| json: integrity valid after concurrency        | PASS   |                                                                       |
| json: tampering detected by verify_integrity   | PASS   | json: INTEGRITY FAILURE - HMAC digest mismatch                        |
| json: tampered data not trusted on access      | PASS   | refused to load on re-open                                            |
| sqlite: all records readable                   | PASS   | 1000/1000                                                             |
| sqlite: login uses the same auth logic         | PASS   |                                                                       |
| sqlite: no concurrency errors                  | PASS   | 0                                                                     |
| sqlite: concurrent updates all applied         | PASS   | counter=20/20                                                         |
| sqlite: integrity valid after concurrency      | PASS   |                                                                       |
| sqlite: tampering detected by verify_integrity | PASS   | sqlite: INTEGRITY FAILURE - record for 'user0000' failed verification |
| sqlite: tampered data not trusted on access    | PASS   | row signature verified on read                                        |
+------------------------------------------------+--------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

Notes:
  - JSON rewrites the whole file on every save (O(n) per write), while SQLite updates one row in a transaction - the insert/update gap grows with account count.
  - JSON detects tampering when the file is loaded or verify_integrity() is called; SQLite verifies each row signature on every read.
  - In-process threading is safe for both backends. JSON is NOT safe across processes without an external file lock; SQLite provides cross-process locking and WAL.
  - The same authentication service was used unchanged against both backends, demonstrating the storage interface works as intended.

RESULT: 14/14 checks passed
